/*
    mSL_Curves.jsfx-inc  (2026-11-24)

    ====================================== The curves ======================================

    The curves of the applications (envelopes and waveforms), shared : from the module "Curves" of Interstys (its_Crv_*).
    Diffusion-3 : the modules "Curves A" ... "D" (the editors, crv_Editor), saved with the project (crv_Serialize, record
    'crv1'), the tables (crv_Frame, @gfx) read by crv_F (@gfx or @block) : the MetaSurfaces, the dynamics of the spatial
    projectors. Interstys (2026-11-24) : the modules "Curves A" ... "H" (crv_Editor), its tables read by its sound (its
    names kept as aliases : its_CrvTab ... ; its_Crv_B(k) = crv_B(k) + 1, the block of Interstys : its records 'crvc' are
    unchanged), its own analysis of the blocks Curve of its settings (its passes) and its own records.

    CRV_MX curves, in static memory (crv_B(k) : its block ; read by @block through its table, without allocation) ; a block :
    [crv_fU] 1 the curve exists, [crv_fT] its type, [crv_fF] its flags (1 : periodic), [crv_fN] its count of points,
    [crv_fSel] the point selected last (the editors), [crv_fSus] the sustain point (-1 : none), then the points (x, y, c) :
    x from 0 to 1 (not decreasing), c the curvature of the segment that starts at the point. Its name : crv_nm[k] (a text,
    "" : none ; case sensitive, 1 ... CRV_NMLEN characters, without double quote).
    The types : the editor shows the part kept (V, x in [0, 1]) ; the complete form F (u in [0, 1]) is deduced by symmetry :
        0 Env   : an envelope, y in [0, 1] ; F = V
        1 Wave  : a waveform, y in [-1, 1] ; F = V
        2 HEnv  : a half envelope, the rise (y in [0, 1]) ; the fall is its mirror : F(u) = V(2 u) for u <= 0.5, V(2 - 2 u) after
        3 QWave : a quarter of a waveform (y in [-1, 1], the first point at (0, 0)) ; its mirror gives the half waveform H,
                  then the complete form as HWave
        4 HWave : a half waveform (y in [-1, 1], the first and the last y : 0) : F(u) = V(2 u) for u <= 0.5, -V(2 - 2 u) after
    The periodic flag : Env and Wave only. The sustain point of an envelope (crv_fSus : its index, -1 : none) divides it in
    the rise and the fall.
    The tables : for each curve, CRV_TN + 1 samples of its complete form F(j / CRV_TN) and CRV_TG guards on each side (a
    cycle : t[-2], t[-1] are t[CRV_TN - 2], t[CRV_TN - 1], t[CRV_TN + 1] is t[1] ; the cubic interpolation of Interstys),
    built by @gfx when the curve changes (crv_Frame : the curve compared with its copy crv_tbc) ; the plateau of an
    envelope (crv_tbXs, crv_tbS : the Grains of Interstys) ; crv_F(k, u) : F(u), linear between the samples (a curve that
    does not exist : 0 ; crv_tbE[k] 0). (2026-11-24 : 4096 samples and the guards of Interstys ; 1024 before.)
    The editors (crv_Editor, the module of the host : its blockId, the editor e = 0 ... CRV_NE - 1) : the state of each one in
    crv_ed (CRV_ES words : 0 the curve shown, 1 the grid, 2 ... 10 the mouse, 11 the curve of the selection), its selected
    points in crv_edSel ; crv_Editor puts the state of the editor drawn in the globals crv_uiK ... crv_selF (crv_EdGet), then
    keeps it (crv_EdPut). The mouse in the graph (crv_Edit) : a clic on a point selects it (moved while the button is down ;
    Shift + clic : the points from the first selected to it ; Cmd + clic : added or removed) ; a clic near the curve between
    two points : a drag up or down bends the segment (a clic without moving : straight) ; a clic elsewhere : a new point ;
    right clic on a point : deleted (a selected point : the selection) ; Shift while moving : fine. Keys over the module :
    d the curve in the log, h the selected point becomes the sustain point (again : none), z Undo, Cmd + A all the points.
    The pad (one line) : 0 the curve (left : the next one, Shift : the previous one ; right : the menu), 1 its name (a
    prompt), 2 its type (left : the next one, Shift : the previous one ; right : the menu), 3 its count of points, 4 periodic
    (Env, Wave), 5 the grid (Off, 4, 8, 16, 32), 6 Undo (again : Redo), 7 Actions (new curves, duplicate, dump, sustain,
    delete ; 2026-11-24 : export this curve, all the curves, as mSL settings).
    (2026-11-24, the user) The marks of the editors on the paths of the host (the MetaSurfaces of Diffusion-3) : the editor
    used last (the mouse over its graph, a clic in the module) and shown in the last frame drawn (crv_MarkE) gives its curve,
    its selected points, the x under the mouse in its graph (crv_hovX) ; crv_Us : the places in the complete form of a point
    of the part edited. The other way (2026-11-24, the user) : the playheads of the host (crv_PhSet : the brush of each
    MetaSurface on its path, the part of its length) are drawn in the graph of that editor (crv_DrawPh) : a vertical line
    at the x of the part edited (crv_XOf), a dot on the curve, a letter ; one that is not set again for 0.5 s : gone.
    (2026-11-24, step 3 of the curves in Diffusion-3) The curves as dynamics (sp_Ease of the spatial projectors and of the
    MetaSurfaces : the code CRV_DYN + k, crv_P : the place 0 ... 1 ; the menus, crv_MenuAdd ; the next one, crv_DynNext ;
    its name, crv_DynName) ; the playheads may belong to a curve (the modulators of the MetaSurfaces : their phase).
    (2026-11-24, step 4) The settings of the curves (crv_TbCurve : a block "Curve id keys..." of the mSL "settings", read by
    the host ; crv_TbCommit : the curves staged, set when the whole analysis is without error) ; the exports (crv_XpCurve :
    the lines of a curve ; crv_Export : a file, see mSL_Export).
    Included twice in @init (static memory ; crv_part) : part 1 (the data, the curves, their tables, the settings) before
    the analysis of the settings of the host (Diffusion-3-Set-Table), after mSL_Utilities, mSL_Strings ; part 2 (the
    editors, the exports, the record of the project) after the UI libraries (ui-lib, mSL_ui_Pads, mSL_Colors,
    ui-lib-JJ-GUI, mSL_ui_LibJJ), mSL_Panes part 1 (keepBlockInfos), mSL_Serialize (save_mem, load_mem, ser_hdr) and
    mSL_Export (xpt_*).
*/

<? crv_part != 1 ? _suppress = 1; ?>

CRV_MX = 64;               // the curves : 1 ... 64 (index 0 ... 63)
CRV_PMX = 128;              // the points of a curve
CRV_NMLEN = 31;             // the characters of a name
crv_fU = 0; crv_fT = 1; crv_fF = 2; crv_fN = 3; crv_fSel = 4; crv_fSus = 5; crv_fP = 6;
CRV_BS = crv_fP + 3 * CRV_PMX;
CRV_ENV = 0; CRV_WAVE = 1; CRV_HENV = 2; CRV_QWAVE = 3; CRV_HWAVE = 4; CRV_NTY = 5;
CRV_PER = 1;                // the flag periodic
crv_blk = make_array(CRV_MX * CRV_BS);
crv_nm = make_array(CRV_MX);
<? i = 0; loop(64, printf("crv_nm[%d] = #crv_nm%d; ", i, i); ((i % 8) == 7) ? printf("\n"); i += 1;); ?>
// the types : their short names (settings, log), their long names (the pad), the order of the cell of the type and of the
// new curves (the envelopes, then the waveforms)
crv_tyN = make_array(CRV_NTY); crv_tyL = make_array(CRV_NTY); crv_tyO = make_array(CRV_NTY);
crv_tyN[0] = "Env"; crv_tyN[1] = "Wave"; crv_tyN[2] = "HEnv"; crv_tyN[3] = "QWave"; crv_tyN[4] = "HWave";
crv_tyL[0] = "Envelope"; crv_tyL[1] = "Waveform"; crv_tyL[2] = "H-Envelope"; crv_tyL[3] = "Q-Waveform"; crv_tyL[4] = "H-Waveform";
crv_tyO[0] = CRV_ENV; crv_tyO[1] = CRV_HENV; crv_tyO[2] = CRV_WAVE; crv_tyO[3] = CRV_QWAVE; crv_tyO[4] = CRV_HWAVE;
// one level of Undo : the curve before the last change (crv_undoK : its number, -1 none ; crv_undoE : 0 if there was no
// curve ; its name #crv_undoN) ; the curve when a gesture starts (crv_preK ..., #crv_preN)
crv_undoB = make_array(CRV_BS); crv_undoK = -1; crv_undoE = 0;
crv_preB = make_array(CRV_BS); crv_preK = -1; crv_preE = 0;
crv_tmpB = make_array(CRV_BS);
// the editors
CRV_NE = 8; CRV_ES = 12;
crv_ed = make_array(CRV_NE * CRV_ES);
crv_edSel = make_array(CRV_NE * CRV_PMX);
i__k = 0; loop(CRV_NE, i__p = crv_ed + i__k * CRV_ES; i__p[0] = i__k; i__p[4] = i__p[11] = -1; i__k += 1;);
crv_selF = crv_edSel; crv_selK = -1;      // the selected points (1) of the curve crv_selK (the editor drawn)
crv_orig = make_array(3 * CRV_PMX);       // the points when a move starts (crv_Move)
crv_uiK = 0;                              // the curve shown by the editor drawn ; its state : see crv_EdGet
crv_mDrag = crv_moved = 0; crv_dragI = -1; // the mouse : 0 nothing, 1 points moved, 2 the curvature of a segment
crv_m0x = crv_m0y = crv_p0x = crv_p0y = crv_c0 = 0;
crv_grid = 0;                             // the grid (x and y) : 0 none, else its count of divisions
crv_gridN = make_array(5); crv_gridN[0] = 0; crv_gridN[1] = 4; crv_gridN[2] = 8; crv_gridN[3] = 16; crv_gridN[4] = 32;
CRV_PAD = 6;                              // the margin of the graph (pixels) : the points at the edges are seen
crv_renK = -1;                            // the curve renamed by the prompt (#crv_ren)
// the tables (see above ; 2026-11-24 : those of Interstys, CRV_TN 4096 samples, CRV_TG guards on each side : the sample 0 of
// the curve k at crv_tab + k * CRV_TS + CRV_TG ; t[-2] t[-1] : t[CRV_TN - 2] t[CRV_TN - 1], t[CRV_TN + 1] : t[1], a cycle for
// the cubic interpolation of Interstys)
CRV_TN = 4096; CRV_TG = 2; CRV_TS = CRV_TN + 2 * CRV_TG;
crv_tab = make_array(CRV_MX * CRV_TS);
crv_tbc = make_array(CRV_MX * CRV_BS);    // the curve when its table was built
crv_tbE = make_array(CRV_MX);             // 1 : the table comes from a curve (0 : zeros)
// (2026-11-24, from Interstys) the plateau of an envelope in its table (the mode Grains of the readers of Interstys) : its x
// (-1 : not an envelope, or no curve) and its level
crv_tbXs = make_array(CRV_MX); crv_tbS = make_array(CRV_MX);
CRV_TBMX = 4;                             // the tables built per run of @gfx at most
crv_tbK = 0;                              // the first curve looked at
crv_sv = make_array(2 * CRV_NE + 4);      // (crv_Serialize)
// (2026-11-24) the marks of the editors (see above) : the last frame (gfx_executed) where each editor drew its graph, the x
// under the mouse in it (-1 : none), the editor used last (-1 : none) ; the places of a point (crv_Us)
crv_seenF = make_array(CRV_NE); crv_hovX = make_array(CRV_NE);
i__k = 0; loop(CRV_NE, crv_seenF[i__k] = -10; crv_hovX[i__k] = -1; i__k += 1;);
crv_lastE = -1; crv_up = make_array(4);
// (2026-11-24) the playheads of the host (crv_PhSet) : the place u in the complete form, the time it was set, the color
// (24 bits), the letter
// (the curve read, -1 : all of them ; a text after the letter)
CRV_PHN = 16;
crv_phU = make_array(CRV_PHN); crv_phT = make_array(CRV_PHN); crv_phC = make_array(CRV_PHN); crv_phL = make_array(CRV_PHN);
crv_phK = make_array(CRV_PHN); crv_phX = make_array(CRV_PHN);
i__k = 0; loop(CRV_PHN, crv_phT[i__k] = -10; i__k += 1;);

// The block of the curve k ; it exists
function crv_B(k) ( crv_blk + max(0, min(CRV_MX - 1, k|0)) * CRV_BS; );
function crv_Ex(k) local(b) ( b = crv_B(k); (k >= 0) && (k < CRV_MX) && (b[crv_fU] > 0); );

// The shape of a segment, t in [0, 1] : t / (t + a (1 - t)), a = CRV_KS^-c (c > 0 : a fast start) ; monotonic ; c and -c
// give mirror shapes
CRV_KS = 1000;
function crv_Shape(t, c) ( (c === 0) ? t : t / (t + (CRV_KS ^ (-c)) * (1 - t)); );

// The value of the curve b at x in [0, 1] (the part edited, V)
function crv_Val(b, x) local(n, p, i, x0, x1)
(
    n = b[crv_fN]; p = b + crv_fP;
    x = max(0, min(1, x));
    i = 0; while ((i < n - 2) && (p[3 * (i + 1)] <= x)) ( i += 1; );
    p += 3 * i; x0 = p[0]; x1 = p[3];
    (x1 <= x0) ? p[4] : p[1] + (p[4] - p[1]) * crv_Shape((x - x0) / (x1 - x0), p[2]);
);

// The lowest y of the type ty : 0 for the envelopes, -1 for the waveforms
function crv_Lo(ty) ( ((ty === CRV_ENV) || (ty === CRV_HENV)) ? 0 : -1; );

// The points of a new curve of type ty (it exists) : Env, HEnv, QWave from (0, 0) to (1, 1) ; Wave at 0 ; HWave (0, 0),
// (0.5, 1), (1, 0)
function crv_Default(b, ty)
(
    memset(b, 0, CRV_BS);
    b[crv_fU] = 1; b[crv_fT] = ty; b[crv_fN] = 2; b[crv_fSel] = -1; b[crv_fSus] = -1;
    b[crv_fP + 3] = 1; b[crv_fP + 4] = (ty === CRV_WAVE) ? 0 : 1;
    (ty === CRV_HWAVE) ? (
        b[crv_fN] = 3;
        b[crv_fP + 3] = 0.5; b[crv_fP + 6] = 1; b[crv_fP + 7] = 0;
    );
);

// The points kept in the bounds of the type ; periodic (Env, Wave) : the last y is the first one ; QWave : the first y 0 ;
// HWave : the first and the last y 0 ; the sustain : a point of an Env
function crv_Clamp(b) local(lo, ty, p)
(
    ty = b[crv_fT] = max(0, min(CRV_NTY - 1, 0|b[crv_fT]));
    b[crv_fN] = max(2, min(CRV_PMX, 0|b[crv_fN]));
    lo = crv_Lo(ty);
    p = b + crv_fP; loop(b[crv_fN], p[0] = max(0, min(1, p[0])); p[1] = max(lo, min(1, p[1])); p[2] = max(-1, min(1, p[2])); p += 3;);
    ((ty !== CRV_ENV) && (ty !== CRV_WAVE)) ? (b[crv_fF] = b[crv_fF] & (-1 ~ CRV_PER));
    (b[crv_fF] & CRV_PER) ? (b[crv_fP + 3 * (b[crv_fN] - 1) + 1] = b[crv_fP + 1]);
    ((ty === CRV_QWAVE) || (ty === CRV_HWAVE)) ? (b[crv_fP + 1] = 0);
    (ty === CRV_HWAVE) ? (b[crv_fP + 3 * (b[crv_fN] - 1) + 1] = 0);
    ((ty !== CRV_ENV) || (b[crv_fSus] < 0) || (b[crv_fSus] >= b[crv_fN])) ? (b[crv_fSus] = -1) : (b[crv_fSus] = floor(b[crv_fSus]));
);

// The values V(j / m) of the curve b in t[0 ... m] (the segments followed in order)
function crv_Fill(b, t, m) local(n, p, q, i, j, x, x0, x1)
(
    n = b[crv_fN]; p = b + crv_fP; i = 0; j = 0;
    loop(m + 1,
        x = j / m;
        while ((i < n - 2) && (p[3 * (i + 1)] <= x)) ( i += 1; );
        q = p + 3 * i; x0 = q[0]; x1 = q[3];
        t[j] = (x1 <= x0) ? q[4] : q[1] + (q[4] - q[1]) * crv_Shape((x - x0) / (x1 - x0), q[2]);
        j += 1;
    );
);

// The table of the curve k : its complete form F(j / CRV_TN), j = 0 ... CRV_TN (the types HEnv, QWave, HWave by symmetry),
// the guards (a cycle) ; zeros if the curve does not exist ; the curve copied into crv_tbc ; the plateau (crv_tbXs, crv_tbS)
function crv_Build(k) local(b, t, n, ty, j, i, p)
(
    b = crv_B(k); t = crv_tab + k * CRV_TS + CRV_TG; n = CRV_TN;
    (b[crv_fU] > 0) ? (
        ty = b[crv_fT];
        (ty === CRV_HENV) ? (
            crv_Fill(b, t, n / 2);
            j = n / 2 + 1; loop(n / 2, t[j] = t[n - j]; j += 1;);
        ) :
        (ty === CRV_HWAVE) ? (
            crv_Fill(b, t, n / 2);
            j = n / 2 + 1; loop(n / 2, t[j] = -t[n - j]; j += 1;);
        ) :
        (ty === CRV_QWAVE) ? (
            crv_Fill(b, t, n / 4);
            j = 0; loop(n / 4, t[n / 2 - j] = t[j]; j += 1;);
            j = n / 2 + 1; loop(n / 2, t[j] = -t[n - j]; j += 1;);
        ) : (
            crv_Fill(b, t, n);
        );
        t[-2] = t[n - 2]; t[-1] = t[n - 1]; t[n + 1] = t[1];
        memcpy(crv_tbc + k * CRV_BS, b, crv_fP + 3 * b[crv_fN]);
        crv_tbE[k] = 1;
        // the plateau (the grains of a reader of Interstys) : an envelope, its sustain point, else its highest point ; a half
        // envelope, its top (u = 0.5) ; a waveform : none
        p = b + crv_fP;
        (ty === CRV_ENV) ? (
            i = b[crv_fSus];
            (i < 0) ? ( i = 0; j = 1; loop(b[crv_fN] - 1, (p[3 * j + 1] > p[3 * i + 1]) ? (i = j); j += 1;); );
            crv_tbXs[k] = p[3 * i]; crv_tbS[k] = p[3 * i + 1];
        ) :
        (ty === CRV_HENV) ? (
            crv_tbXs[k] = 0.5; crv_tbS[k] = t[n / 2];
        ) : (
            crv_tbXs[k] = -1; crv_tbS[k] = 1;
        );
    ) : (
        memset(t - CRV_TG, 0, CRV_TS);
        memset(crv_tbc + k * CRV_BS, 0, crv_fP);
        crv_tbE[k] = 0;
        crv_tbXs[k] = -1; crv_tbS[k] = 1;
    );
);
// the table of the curve k is no more that of the curve (its existence, its type, its points)
function crv_TbDiff(k) local(b, c, n, i, d)
(
    b = crv_B(k); c = crv_tbc + k * CRV_BS;
    (b[crv_fU] <= 0) ? (d = crv_tbE[k]) :
    !crv_tbE[k] ? (d = 1) : (
        n = b[crv_fN];
        d = (b[crv_fT] !== c[crv_fT]) || (n !== c[crv_fN]) || (b[crv_fSus] !== c[crv_fSus]); // (the sustain : the plateau)
        i = crv_fP; loop(d ? 0 : 3 * n, (b[i] !== c[i]) ? (d = 1); i += 1;);
    );
    d;
);
// @gfx, each run (even when the window is closed) : the tables of the curves that changed (CRV_TBMX at most ; the next run
// goes on after the last one built)
function crv_Frame() local(k, m, i)
(
    m = 0; i = 0;
    while ((i < CRV_MX) && (m < CRV_TBMX)) (
        k = (crv_tbK + i) % CRV_MX;
        crv_TbDiff(k) ? ( crv_Build(k); m += 1; (m === CRV_TBMX) ? (crv_tbK = (k + 1) % CRV_MX); );
        i += 1;
    );
);
// F(u) of the curve k (u in [0, 1] ; its table : linear between the samples ; no curve : 0), @gfx or @block
function crv_F(k, u) local(t, x, i)
(
    ((k >= 0) && (k < CRV_MX)) ? (
        t = crv_tab + (k|0) * CRV_TS + CRV_TG;
        x = max(0, min(1, u)) * CRV_TN; i = min(CRV_TN - 1, floor(x));
        t[i] + (x - i) * (t[i + 1] - t[i]);
    ) : 0;
);

// (2026-11-24) The places u in the complete form F of the point x of the part edited (V) of a curve of type ty, into crv_up ;
// returns their count (Env, Wave : 1 ; HEnv, HWave : 2, the second one in the mirror ; QWave : 4)
function crv_Us(ty, x)
(
    ((ty === CRV_HENV) || (ty === CRV_HWAVE)) ? ( crv_up[0] = x / 2; crv_up[1] = 1 - x / 2; 2; ) :
    (ty === CRV_QWAVE) ? ( crv_up[0] = x / 4; crv_up[1] = 0.5 - x / 4; crv_up[2] = 0.5 + x / 4; crv_up[3] = 1 - x / 4; 4; ) :
    ( crv_up[0] = x; 1; );
);
// (2026-11-24) The x in the part edited (V) of the place u of the complete form F of a curve of type ty (HEnv, HWave : the
// second half goes back ; QWave : each quarter goes forth, back, forth, back)
function crv_XOf(ty, u) local(q, g)
(
    u = max(0, min(1, u));
    ((ty === CRV_HENV) || (ty === CRV_HWAVE)) ? ( (u <= 0.5) ? 2 * u : 2 - 2 * u; ) :
    (ty === CRV_QWAVE) ? ( q = 4 * u; g = min(3, floor(q)); (g & 1) ? 1 - (q - g) : q - g; ) :
    u;
);
// (2026-11-24) The playhead i (0 ... CRV_PHN - 1) of the host at the place u (0 ... 1) of the complete form, its color c
// (24 bits), its letter l (a character) and the text x after it, the curve k it reads (-1 : all of them) ; to be set again
// at each run of @gfx (else gone after 0.5 s)
function crv_PhSet(i, u, c, l, x, k)
(
    ((i >= 0) && (i < CRV_PHN)) ? (
        crv_phU[i] = max(0, min(1, u)); crv_phC[i] = c; crv_phL[i] = l; crv_phX[i] = x; crv_phK[i] = k;
        crv_phT[i] = time_precise();
    );
);

// (2026-11-24) The editor whose marks the host shows : the one used last if it drew its graph in the last frame drawn (or in
// this one), else the first one that did ; -1 : none
function crv_MarkE() local(e, r)
(
    r = -1;
    ((crv_lastE >= 0) && (crv_lastE < CRV_NE) && (crv_seenF[crv_lastE] >= gfx_executed - 1)) ? (r = crv_lastE) : (
        e = 0;
        while ((r < 0) && (e < CRV_NE)) ( (crv_seenF[e] >= gfx_executed - 1) ? (r = e); e += 1; );
    );
    r;
);

// (2026-11-24, step 3) The curve k as a place (0 ... 1) at u : the dynamics of the motions (sp_Ease, the code CRV_DYN + k) ;
// the envelopes (Env, HEnv) as they are, the waveforms from [-1, 1] to [0, 1] ; no curve : u (linear) ; @gfx or @block (the
// type : that of its table, crv_tbc)
CRV_DYN = 100;
function crv_P(k, u) local(ty)
(
    k = k|0;
